WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.433
GPS does not send a
full calendar date.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.433
Older signals stored that
week number in ten bits.

00:00:05.733 --> 00:00:08.233
The range ends at 1,023.

00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:10.633
At the limit, there
is no new number left.

00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:13.400
Zero is sent again when
the next week begins.

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:16.567
Old software read zero
as the previous cycle.

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:18.733
Their displayed date
jumped backward.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.867
Real time kept
moving forward.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.767
An update selected
the correct GPS cycle.

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:26.200
Now the receiver shows
the correct date.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.467
The number repeated.
Time did not.
